    {
      "id": "ZCsqW-wSnGetzS2xJM95d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -29892.289295146566,
      "y": 7858.405422264525,
      "width": 1245.6706715027979,
      "height": 206.8558936162672,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 746458934,
      "version": 711,
      "versionNonce": 1878372010,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794308872070,
      "created": 1794308777084,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Step | Function | Rows it builds |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | contract_id_of | Contract ID. Without one, the contract can't be stored. |\n| 2 | add_contract | contract |\n| 3 | add_parties | organization (shared), facility (shared), contract_party |\n| 4 | add_document | contract_document: file name, SHA-256, pages, and all three raw answers as JSON (extraction_json) |\n| 5 | add_calendar | pricing_period: one row per period, computed from the term dates and period type |\n| 6 | add_frequencies | contract_change_frequency, contract_change_frequency_period (e.g. quarterly → P1, P4, P7, P10) |\n| 7 | select_baseline | Picks the printed cost model for each product's first pricing period, if the contract prints one |\n| 8 | add_products | product (shared), contract_product, component (shared), contract_product_component, pricing_term, pricing_term_index_leg, pricing_term_tier, market_index (shared), price_build_step \n| 9 | add_adjustments | contract_adjustment, contract_adjustment_tier |\n| 10 | add_freight | facility (plants and distribution centers), freight_bracket, freight_lane, freight_rate. A schedule row that names no product becomes one lane per product, and rates are stored as printed. |\n| 11 | add_cost_model | cost_model (type CONTRACT_BASELINE), cost_model_line, cost_model_freight. The printed totals are recomputed from the build steps and compared within a tolerance of 0.01. |\n| 12 | check_rows | Blocking problems: a required value missing, a code that isn't in the lookup lists, a link to a row that isn't there, or a duplicate key |\n| 13 | check_numbers | Points to check (informational): a number the model read that doesn't appear anywhere in the PDF text |",
      "fontSize": 11.032314326200911,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Step | Function | Rows it builds |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | contract_id_of | Contract ID. Without one, the contract can't be stored. |\n| 2 | add_contract | contract |\n| 3 | add_parties | organization (shared), facility (shared), contract_party |\n| 4 | add_document | contract_document: file name, SHA-256, pages, and all three raw answers as JSON (extraction_json) |\n| 5 | add_calendar | pricing_period: one row per period, computed from the term dates and period type |\n| 6 | add_frequencies | contract_change_frequency, contract_change_frequency_period (e.g. quarterly → P1, P4, P7, P10) |\n| 7 | select_baseline | Picks the printed cost model for each product's first pricing period, if the contract prints one |\n| 8 | add_products | product (shared), contract_product, component (shared), contract_product_component, pricing_term, pricing_term_index_leg, pricing_term_tier, market_index (shared), price_build_step \n| 9 | add_adjustments | contract_adjustment, contract_adjustment_tier |\n| 10 | add_freight | facility (plants and distribution centers), freight_bracket, freight_lane, freight_rate. A schedule row that names no product becomes one lane per product, and rates are stored as printed. |\n| 11 | add_cost_model | cost_model (type CONTRACT_BASELINE), cost_model_line, cost_model_freight. The printed totals are recomputed from the build steps and compared within a tolerance of 0.01. |\n| 12 | check_rows | Blocking problems: a required value missing, a code that isn't in the lookup lists, a link to a row that isn't there, or a duplicate key |\n| 13 | check_numbers | Points to check (informational): a number the model read that doesn't appear anywhere in the PDF text |",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
